{
	"Name": "Okta - Authentication & Sessions - Okta Admin Console Access via Anonymizing Proxy",
	"Description": "Alert: Okta\nGroup: Authentication & Sessions\nMITRE ATT&CK: Initial Access / T1078.004\nSchedule: every 15 minutes over the previous 15 minutes (edit the scheduled search to change it)\nTuning: okta_user_allowlist / okta_ip_allowlist keys \"<login without domain>|Okta Admin Console Access via Anonymizing Proxy\" or \"<ip>|Okta Admin Console Access via Anonymizing Proxy\"\n\nAccess to the Okta Admin Console (user.session.access_admin_app) that Okta flags as coming through an anonymizing proxy (securityContext.isProxy or risk reason \"Anonymizing Proxy\"). Administrators should not need anonymizing proxies; this is a strong sign of a compromised admin account.\n\nReference(s):\n- https://detection.fyi/sigmahq/sigma/identity/okta/okta_admin_activity_from_proxy_query/\n- https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/master/rules/identity/okta/okta_admin_activity_from_proxy_query.yml",
	"GUID": "1d066b02-465e-5993-a0a6-dfde9ff76d22",
